{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 complete — fix landed for review as Gerrit change 1965\n\n### RED oracle (held out from the implementer)\n\n`tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py::test_gate_cost_does_not_scale_with_store_size`, parametrized\nover 4 and 40 tickets. It asserts the ALGORITHMIC property the acceptance criteria ask for — a\nrepeat gate probe on a quiet store reduces NO tickets — rather than a wall clock, which is the\nflake class this bug's own measurements exhibited (and which `scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py`\nblocks anyway).\n\nObserved RED before any fix existed, failing for the right reason at both sizes:\n\n```\nAssertionError: repeat gate probe reduced 4 tickets at n=4\nAssertionError: repeat gate probe reduced 40 tickets at n=40\n```\n\nThe count tracking N is itself the mechanism. The test file was moved OUT of the implementing\nsubagent's tree; it was handed only the proven root cause and a contract card, and it never saw\nthe assertions. The tests were verified byte-identical afterwards.\n\n**Mutation checks — the tests have teeth.** Re-introducing the exact root cause (deleting the\nfast-path early return) returned the primary test to RED with the same message. Separately\nremoving the `_append` invalidation returned `test_queue_mutations_invalidate_the_gate_marker`\nto RED. Restored after each.\n\n### The fix\n\n`src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py` only — `enrich_drain.py` is untouched, so the gate's caller,\nits budget warning and its Windows/never-raise contract are unchanged.\n\nA marker `.rebar/enrich-gate.json` holds `{next_eligible_ns, written_ns}`. `pending_enrichment`\nreturns `[]` immediately when a live marker proves the store quiet; otherwise it runs the\nexisting single scan and, in that same pass, records the soonest instant any live entry could\nbecome pending. Invalidation sits in `_append`, the one funnel for ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE.\n\nSelf-healing, three independent ways: the marker can only ever say \"nothing is pending\" (it can\nnever manufacture work, so a wrong marker costs a delayed drain and never a wrong one); any\nqueue append clears it; and it expires after 10 minutes, well inside the 60-minute default soak,\nso a crash between the append and the clear defers a drain rather than losing it. Every read and\nwrite is best-effort — absent, empty, truncated, non-JSON, wrong-typed and unwritable `.rebar`\nall degrade to the full scan. Writes are atomic (temp file + `os.replace`).\n\n### Replication on the real store\n\n4,835 ticket dirs, load average 27.5, real code path, quiet-store clock:\n\n```\nprobe 0:  2470.472 ms   <- cold, rebuilds the marker\nprobe 1:     0.071 ms\nprobe 2:     0.045 ms\nprobe 3:     0.034 ms\nprobe 4:     0.119 ms\nprobe 5:     0.060 ms\n```\n\nA ~35,000x reduction, and three orders of magnitude INSIDE the 20 ms budget rather than 25x\noutside it.\n\n### Honest limitation — this store will KEEP warning until 3198 is fixed\n\nThe AC \"the WARNING no longer fires on an ordinary write\" is **not yet observable on this\nstore**, and that is not a defect in this fix. `pending_enrichment` currently returns 3 entries\nthat are genuinely pending:\n\n```\n8625-7bea-67db-4cdc   9305-b42c-3262-4c58   e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2\n```\n\nThe fast path correctly refuses to engage while real work is queued — a marker that could\nsuppress a probe with work outstanding would be the far worse bug. Those three are wedged\nbecause of a **separate defect**, now filed as `conscious-weighable-spittlebug`\n(`3198-438c-72a5-470f`, linked `discovered_from` this ticket):\n`enrich_drain._spawn_detached_drain` passes no `cwd=`, so the detached drain child inherits the\ncaller's working directory; when that was a since-removed worktree, `Path.cwd()` raises\n`FileNotFoundError` inside `queue.claim` and the drain dies before claiming anything.\n`.rebar/logs/enrich-drain.log` shows this for four distinct removed worktrees.\n\nOnce 3198 lands and those three drain, this store becomes quiet and the warning stops. The\nmechanism is proven independently by the replication above.\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` PASS. `make typecheck` PASS (598 files). `check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n`active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`. `pytest tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py\ntests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py` 55 passed. Plan review certified (`verdict: certified`,\n`currency_basis: file_impact`) — required because the fix is 164 non-test diff lines, over the\nbugfix-size gate's 150 floor.\n\n### Sibling sweep\n\n**Construct axis.** Swept every `os.listdir(tracker)` in `src/rebar` (18 sites). The specific\nconstruct — a per-ticket multi-`listdir` reduction driven from the hot write path behind a\ncheapness contract — has exactly one instance, the one fixed. The rest are legitimately\nwhole-store operations (fsck, export, graph, reducer, identity, resolver) and are not on a\nbudgeted path. Two notes: `_store/staging.py` already defends the same class with\n`_SWEEP_SCAN_LIMIT`, i.e. this class was recognised elsewhere; and `enrich_drain._stale_digest_ids`\nis a second O(ticket-count) walk with a per-ticket freshness check, but it runs inside `drain()`\nin the detached child, off the write path and with no budget — observed, accepted, not fixed.\n\n**Parity axis.** The rule: \"the write-path drain gate must not do work proportional to store\nsize.\" Channel census — CLI, MCP, library facade and automated callers all reach the store\nthrough `_store/event_append.py`, and both write-path entries (`event_append.py:399` and the\ndual-direction `push.py:497`) call the same `maybe_drain` -> `pending_enrichment` core, so all\ninherit the fix from one site. `rebar enrich status` and `drain()` itself walk the store too, but\nthey are explicit operator/background operations outside the rule. No MISSING slot.\n\n### Caller-dependency gate\n\n`pending_enrichment` has two production callers, both in `enrich_drain.py` (the gate at :366 and\n`drain` at :266). Its signature, return type, sort order and answers are unchanged — only its\nspeed — so both are incidental, not behavioural, dependencies. `drain`'s use stays correct\nbecause its self-heal `enqueue` calls run through `_append` and therefore clear the marker before\nit probes. No pre-existing test was weakened, skipped or deleted; the 15 pre-existing tests in\nthese two files pass unmodified.\n\n### Residual risk\n\n- **`enrich_drain._stale_digest_ids`** — O(ticket count) with per-ticket digest freshness checks\n  (`src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py:222`). ACCEPTED: it runs in the detached drain child, off the\n  write path, with no latency budget, and only when work is genuinely queued.\n- **Mixed rebar versions during rollout** — an older rebar appends queue events without clearing\n  the marker. ACCEPTED: this is exactly what the TTL bounds, to a <=10-minute deferred drain.\n- **The gate-snapshot store** (`smart-disloyal-naga`) — `du -sh` on\n  `$TMPDIR/rebar-gate-snapshots` (63,713 entries) did not complete in 10 minutes, and it is a\n  measured contributor to the vnode saturation (condition D, x1.55). Already ticketed there."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787261024659845001,"uuid":"e56406be-0325-495f-8fc4-b6d19a747973"}